# File & Folder Naming Convention

This project enforces **kebab-case** for all files and folders by default.

## Global Rules (Strict)

- All file and folder names MUST use **kebab-case**
- Use **lowercase letters only**
- Separate words with hyphens (`-`)
- This rule applies to the entire project

### Examples (Correct)

- `user-profile-card.tsx`
- `use-auth-session.ts`
- `api-client.ts`
- `date-format-utils.ts`

### Examples (Incorrect)

- `UserProfileCard.tsx`
- `userProfileCard.tsx`
- `user_profile_card.tsx`

## Exceptions (Rare & Intentional)

- Route files MAY deviate only when required by the framework
- Examples: `page.tsx`, `layout.tsx`, `route.ts`
- Do not introduce PascalCase or camelCase unless the framework requires it
- When in doubt, default to **kebab-case**

## Code vs File Naming

- File names: **k**ebab-case\*\*
- Component and function names in code may use PascalCase or camelCase

---

# App Router Structure (Next.js)

The application follows a strict and intentional route-group structure.

`(marketing)`

- Public, non-authenticated pages
- Landing pages, homepage, pricing, SEO pages

`(platform)`

- Internal platform pages

  `(auth)`
  - Authentication-related pages only
  - Login, register, password reset, email verification

  `(workspace)`
  - Main logged-in product experience
  - Orders, products, user account / profile
  - Future team and organization features

Rules:

- Do not mix concerns between route groups
- Marketing must not depend on platform code
- Auth must stay isolated from workspace features
- Workspace contains all product functionality

---

# Components Architecture

All reusable components live inside `/components`.

## General Rules

- Every component MUST live in its own folder
- Folder name and main file name MUST match
- Use kebab-case for both

Example:
`components/new-sidebar/new-sidebar.tsx`

## /components/ui

- Contains only components generated or modified by shadcn/ui
- Do not add custom business components here

## /components/typography

- Add only if needed
- Prefer native HTML elements first
- Avoid over-abstraction

## Custom Components

- All new custom components go inside /components
- One folder per component
- No misc or common dumping folders

## UI components policy

- All new pages and components MUST use shadcn/ui components as the default UI foundation
- Prefer composing existing shadcn components over creating custom UI from scratch
- Custom UI components should only be created when:
- shadcn does not provide the needed primitive, or
- the design clearly requires deviation
- If shadcn/ui is not installed or missing a required component:
  - Ask the developer for confirmation before installing or generating shadcn components
  - Do NOT auto-install or modify shadcn setup without explicit approval

## Dependency & tooling changes

Any change that introduces:

- new UI libraries
- shadcn installation
- design system changes

MUST be confirmed with the developer before proceeding

# Tailwind CSS v4 Configuration

This project uses **Tailwind CSS v4**. When writing code, use Tailwind CSS v4 syntax and features.

## Key Points:

- Use Tailwind CSS v4 utilities and syntax
- The project uses `@tailwindcss/postcss` v4 for PostCSS integration
- Follow Tailwind CSS v4 documentation patterns
- Use modern CSS-first configuration approach where applicable

## When suggesting Tailwind classes:

- Use v4-compatible class names and utilities
- Prefer v4 syntax over v3 patterns
- Reference Tailwind CSS v4 documentation for new features
